{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Elohim remembered Abraham and sent out Lot</b>. The sense of this verse is that Lot joined the righteous man to go about with him throughout the land, wherever he would go, as it is stated (Genesis 12:4), \"And Lot went with him\" — he went at his command, and therefore he had merit to be saved in the merit of Abraham, for on his account he dwelt in Sodom; and had it not been for Abraham, he would still have been in Haran with his kindred, and it is impossible that harm should come to him on account of Abraham, who went forth at the command of his Maker. This too was the reason Abraham risked his life to pursue the kings on his behalf."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:19.828327780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}